WF-43 — Post-Consultation Handler

## Summary

- Purpose: Handles `consultation_closed` user activity. Interactive button taps route directly (done / rebook / feedback). Free-form text is classified via WF-25 (which owns the safety net), then routed: rebook → WF-45, feedback → WF-44, stop_intent → no extra (clarifier already sent by WF-25), else a Gemini contextual reply.
- Inputs (WF-01 canonical envelope §2.1): `phoneNumber` (top-level), `messageType` (text|interactive), `messageContent`, `rawMessage` (for interactive payloads), `user.{id, status, current_consultation_id, slack_channel_id}`.
- Outputs: routes to WF-44 / WF-45; a thank-you (btn_done) via WF-50 + Slack notification via WF-51; a feedback prompt; or a Gemini-generated reply.
- State Transitions: none directly (downstream WFs may transition).
- Calls Sub-Workflows: WF-25 (Intent Classifier + Safety-Net Hub), WF-44 (Feedback Recorder), WF-45 (Rebook), WF-53 (U1 — on the local Gemini reply's failure), WF-61 (U2 — off-topic counting/block, safety-net §12/D6), WF-50 (Send WhatsApp), WF-51 (Send Slack — btn_done notification).
- **Deltas vs the prior WF-43 (safety-net §6, D5):**
  - stop_intent NO LONGER auto-routes to WF-47 — WF-25 sends the clarifier and returns the intent; WF-43 takes no extra action on stop_intent (removes the live inconsistency + the false-positive unsubscribe risk).
  - REMOVED the inline Gemini-error halt-and-notify chain → on the general-reply Gemini failure, call U1.
  - **D6 (safety-net §12, 2026-05-31):** the general-reply Gemini now returns JSON `{ valid_user_message, response }`. Off-topic-but-legitimate messages (`valid_user_message=false`) — which WF-25 passes through as `general_enquiry` and were previously uncounted — are now logged + counted + blockable via U2/WF-61 (`reason='off_topic'`, `blockThreshold=10`, `blockReason='threshold_off_topic'`). Parse is fail-open (malformed/missing → treat as valid). Closes the previously-unbounded off-topic cost vector without a second classify call (the response Gemini emits the relevance flag for free).
    - **Interplay with BUG-06c (§13):** D6 handles ONLY the legit pass-through buckets (`general_enquiry`/`wants_consultation`) that WF-25 returns. *Garbage* is handled + counted by WF-25 and stopped before Step 12 (WF-25 emits 0 items, §13) — so D6's off_topic check never sees garbage. The pre-§13 symptoms (a 2nd message on garbage + a null-content `off_topic` row + the garbage/off_topic double-count) are resolved by §13. The two amendments are complementary: §13 keeps garbage out; D6 counts the legit-but-off-topic remainder.
- **Notes:**
  - Interactive button cascade is unchanged.
  - Copy reuse-existing — verify verbatim at build.

---

## Algorithm

Step 1: Start — triggered by WF-02 for a `consultation_closed` user. Read the WF-01 canonical envelope.
Step 2: Check: `messageType == 'interactive'` (a button reply)?
  - If YES → go to Step 3.
  - If NO → go to Step 8.
Step 3: Inspect `rawMessage.interactive.button_reply.id`:
  - "btn_done" → go to Step 5.
  - "btn_rebook" → go to Step 4.
  - otherwise (btn_feedback or any other id) → go to Step 7.
Step 4: Call WF-45 (Rebook) with `phoneNumber`, `userId`. End.
Step 5: Send the close-thanks — call WF-50 with `{ phoneNumber, messageType: 'text', messageContent: "Thank you for choosing Chinmay Astro. We hope to see you again — just send REBOOK whenever you're ready.\n\nYou can also email chinmay_astro@gmail.com anytime if you need anything we can't help with here, or reply STOP if you'd prefer to unsubscribe." }`.
Step 6: Notify admin — call WF-51 with `{ channelId: user.slack_channel_id, messageText: "✅ User tapped \"Done, thanks\" — conversation closed. Channel stays open for any future rebook." }`. No state change. End.
Step 7: Prompt for feedback — call WF-50 with `{ phoneNumber, messageType: 'text', messageContent: "✍️ Thanks for choosing to share your feedback! Please type your thoughts about the consultation and send them — we appreciate every word!" }`. End.
Step 8: Call WF-25 with `{ phoneNumber, userId: user.id, messageContent, userStatus: user.status, userName: user.name, slackChannelId: user.slack_channel_id }`. Receive `intentResult`. **Garbage / abuse do not continue here — mechanism (BUG-06c, safety-net §13):** WF-25 emits **0 items** (its Step 13 `Return Nothing`); this handler's `Call WF-25` has `alwaysOutputData=false`, so 0 items → Step 9 onward skip. So the only intents that reach the Gemini reply (Step 12) are the pass-through buckets (`general_enquiry` / `wants_consultation`) — NOT garbage. Before BUG-06c, WF-25 returned 1 item on garbage and this handler wrongly ran its Gemini reply on it (2nd message + a null-content `off_topic` count). Do not remove WF-25's `Return Nothing`. (Gemini-failure still terminates via U1's halt.)
Step 9: Check: `intentResult == 'stop_intent'`?
  - If YES → End (WF-25 already sent the clarifier; no extra — D5).
  - If NO → go to Step 10.
Step 10: Check: `intentResult == 'rebook_intent'`?
  - If YES → call WF-45 (Rebook) with `phoneNumber`, `userId`. End.
  - If NO → go to Step 11.
Step 11: Check: `intentResult == 'feedback_intent'`?
  - If YES → call WF-44 (Feedback Recorder) with `phoneNumber`, `userId`, `messageContent`. End.
  - If NO → go to Step 12.
Step 12: Build the general-reply Gemini prompt (safety-net §12.6 verbatim) — the prompt OPENS with the JSON mandate (front-loaded for determinism, D6c) then the greeting/question/off-topic-aware welcome-back guidance (answer any genuine question briefly; warmly steer re-engaging users to reply REBOOK for a new ₹500 reading; for off-topic-but-legitimate messages gently acknowledge + steer back; never tell a closed user to "confirm payment"). Append the user's message. POST to Gemini (gemini-2.5-flash-lite, temperature=0.3, `generationConfig.responseMimeType='application/json'`). On Gemini API failure → go to Step 17. On success → go to Step 13.
Step 13: Parse the JSON response into `{ valid_user_message, response }`. **Fail-open (D6e):** if parsing fails or either field is missing/malformed, set `valid_user_message=true` and `response=` best-effort text (or a safe default welcome-back reply). Never block or silence a user on a parse glitch.
Step 14: Check: `valid_user_message === false`?
  - If NO (true / fail-open) → go to Step 16 (send the reply).
  - If YES → go to Step 15.
Step 15: (off-topic — count + block check, D6) Call U2/WF-61 with `{ phoneNumber, messageType: 'text', reason: 'off_topic', messageContent, blockThreshold: 10, blockReason: 'threshold_off_topic' }`. Receive `{ blocked }`.
  - If `blocked === true` → End (silent — U2 already set `status=blocked` and sent the admin block alert; no reply, D6a).
  - If `blocked === false` → go to Step 16 (still send the graceful redirect reply, D6a).
Step 16: Send the reply — call WF-50 with `{ phoneNumber, messageType: 'text', messageContent: <response> }`. End.
Step 17: Gemini API failure — call U1 with `{ phoneNumber, userFacing: true, consultChannelId: user.slack_channel_id, context: { source: 'WF-43', userName: user.name, userStateText: 'consultation completed', userMessage: messageContent, errorDetail: <summary> } }`. End.
